<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: One killed as fishing boats collide off Ireland.</title>
<headline>One killed as fishing boats collide off Ireland.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>One man was killed and two others were injured on Sunday when two fishing boats collided off the southern tip of Ireland, coastguards said.</p>
<p>&quot;An Irish fishing vessel, the Exodus, was in a collision with the English-registered Sea Horse which is manned by a Spanish crew,&quot; said a coastguard spokesman.</p>
<p>&quot;The circumstances are still vague. The weather was reasonable and there was good visibility,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>The spokesman said an investigation would be launched to determine the cause of the collision.</p>
</text>
